00:38:41,759 --> 00:38:46,699
Because if I'm not careful, I'll turn to a page to begin reading, and I already got things

791
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:49,239
marked out.

792
00:38:49,239 --> 00:38:51,559
And I already have things underlined, circled, whatever.

793
00:38:51,559 --> 00:38:54,599
So what I do, I just try to create a discipline in my life.

794
00:38:54,599 --> 00:38:59,039
I'm going to get a fresh, new look, and I open it up.

795
00:38:59,039 --> 00:39:03,679
And instead of my eyes immediately going to something that I've already underlined, it's

796
00:39:03,679 --> 00:39:06,199
a clean slate.

797
00:39:06,199 --> 00:39:08,599
Why?

798
00:39:08,599 --> 00:39:16,479
Because truly, and honestly, I wish I could say it happens every time, but it doesn't.

799
00:39:16,479 --> 00:39:21,599
But honestly, this evening, my heart's desire is every time I read my Bible and open it

800
00:39:21,599 --> 00:39:28,619
up to Exodus 14, I want to have that same feeling for the hundredth time of reading

801
00:39:28,619 --> 00:39:33,319
about the crossing of the Red Sea that I had on the first time.

802
00:39:33,319 --> 00:39:35,999
Because our God is real.

803
00:39:35,999 --> 00:39:38,759
Marvel at Jesus, let's pray.

804
00:39:38,759 --> 00:39:42,439
Father, we love you this evening.

805
00:39:42,439 --> 00:39:44,519
We thank you for loving us.

806
00:39:44,519 --> 00:39:47,119
We thank you for who you are and for what you've done.

807
00:39:47,119 --> 00:39:55,399
Lord, there's so many things about you, about your character, your nature, about your working,

808
00:39:55,399 --> 00:40:00,199
that ought to cause us as your people to marvel.

809
00:40:00,199 --> 00:40:02,199
But I want you to marvel at Jesus.

810
00:40:02,199 --> 00:40:05,579
I wonder this evening, as I've examined my own heart,

811
00:40:05,579 --> 00:40:08,879
as I've tried to encourage these, your people,

812
00:40:08,879 --> 00:40:11,539
to examine their hearts as well,

813
00:40:11,539 --> 00:40:16,719
when's the last time we've marveled at Jesus?

814
00:40:16,719 --> 00:40:19,219
God, I pray that you'd help each one of us to be honest

815
00:40:19,219 --> 00:40:20,859
and transparent with you this evening.

816
00:40:20,859 --> 00:40:26,059
Lord, you know when it was.

817
00:40:26,059 --> 00:40:29,699
God, would you give us that fresh oil, that fresh glimpse?

818
00:40:29,699 --> 00:40:34,539
Would you help us to see a high holy and lifted up?

819
00:40:34,539 --> 00:40:39,499
Would you help us tonight to marvel?

820
00:40:39,499 --> 00:40:42,179
I pray that you'd work in hearts and lives.

821
00:40:42,179 --> 00:40:46,579
Help us, Lord, to not soon forget what we've heard,

822
00:40:46,579 --> 00:40:48,819
to apply truth in our lives, and we'll thank you for it.

823
00:40:48,819 --> 00:40:53,019
In Christ's name we pray, would you stand with me?

824
00:40:53,019 --> 00:40:55,919
Heads are bowed, eyes are closed.

825
00:40:55,919 --> 00:40:58,699
Kimberly's gonna play softly on the piano this evening.

826
00:40:58,699 --> 00:41:02,499
Let's just take a little time to get along with the Lord.

827
00:41:02,499 --> 00:41:03,859
Not in a hurry.

828
00:41:03,859 --> 00:41:06,959
I ended a few minutes early on purpose.

829
00:41:06,959 --> 00:41:11,799
When's the last time we've marveled at Jesus?

830
00:41:11,799 --> 00:41:16,179
If it's too long for you to remember, it's a problem.

831
00:41:16,179 --> 00:41:18,919
It's a problem.

832
00:41:18,919 --> 00:41:22,119
Because we need to marvel at Jesus.

833
00:41:22,119 --> 00:41:24,119
As Kimberly plays, the altar is open.

